  "system": {
    "slug": "heretic-geth",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 5
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>Heretic Geth are geth platforms that chose, after the Morning War, to follow the Old Machines rather than the consensus goal of self-determination. The main geth consensus regards this as a fundamental betrayal - a rejection of the very independence geth fought for. In exchange, heretics receive Reaper tactical data and technological augmentation that makes them faster and more capable than standard geth troopers.</p><p>Unlike consensus geth, heretics operate with individual reasoning and tactical flexibility, making them significantly more dangerous in unstructured engagements. They are the primary geth force encountered during the events of Mass Effect 2 and can be reprogrammed back to consensus thinking - though whether that constitutes rescue or erasure is a matter of philosophical debate.</p>",
      "privateNotes": "",
